0..75 Comment "//! A bridge `Bridge(A, a, b)` relates two points of `A` parametrically, as"
76..106 Comment "//! the bridge fold reads `A`."
107..110 Comment "//!"
111..188 Comment "//! A path identifies its endpoints, and a bridge only relates them. A bridge"
189..266 Comment "//! at the universe is a relation between two types, and one at a type former"
267..343 Comment "//! lifts the relations of its parts. A bridge has no reflexivity, transport"
344..373 Comment "//! or eliminator of its own."
374..377 Comment "//!"
378..457 Comment "//! An introduction checked at a bridge checks at the fibre the fold reads from"
458..535 Comment "//! the carrier and the endpoints. The fold reads a list cell by cell, a base"
536..612 Comment "//! type or a sum as its identity, and a function code by extensionality. An"
613..668 Comment "//! atom stating an identity system bears its relation."
669..672 Comment "//!"
673..744 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/identity/bridge.gandr` — the bridges refused"
745..792 Comment "//! - see: #3519 — the model laws of the fold"
793..869 Comment "//! - cites: [Cavallo-2021-internal_parametricity_cubical_type_theory], § 3"
870..873 Comment "//!"
874..1047 Comment "//! [Cavallo-2021-internal_parametricity_cubical_type_theory]: https://doi.org/10.46298/lmcs-17(4:5)2021 \"Cavallo and Harper, Internal parametricity for cubical type theory\""
